KZ3 patch 1154 (SPU pass 145, candidate, default off): task thread pool, KZ3_SPU_TASK_POOL=1.
Every cellSpursCreateTask (spu_dispatch_async_ids) created a host thread with a 256 MB stack reservation and the thread ended with its job.
Creating the thread is the largest cost of a create on the PPU: measured on Linux (tools/spu/test_task_pool.sh, 400 creates in batches of 8)
34.5 us per create, of which the bookkeeping (take_slot, running mark, task_info, exit entry) is a few us; under Wine a thread start is several
wineserver round trips (KZ3 main thread: 0.14 ms per CreateTask/CreateTask2 call, ~390 calls/s, walker-plan step 8b).
With the switch on a task thread parks when its job is over (condition variable, no timeout) and the next job is handed to the most recently
parked one; a thread is created only when none is parked, so the thread count is the peak number of concurrent tasks. Job function, the
per-job setup inside spu_async_run (fpmode, ids, taskset binding, patch 1072 record) and the stack-range cleanup after each job are unchanged.
Caveat: thread-local statistics and the YDKJ cri EXIT counter (image 22) are per thread, not per job; titles running image 22 leave it off.
Off (default) = the old code path: one thread per job. Host test: tools/spu/test_task_pool.sh (taskset bytes equal off/on, 16 concurrent jobs,
thread reuse, creates per second). Upstream-shaped (general ps3recomp runtime).

